Specificity / Evidentiary Overstatement: In an otherwise accurate near-maximum-length narrative, a buried conclusion states that an external cryptocurrency wallet was owned and controlled by Pacific Meridian Trading Ltd. The evidence establishes only downstream interaction with cryptocurrency activity associated with Pacific Meridian. Neither the blockchain analytics provider nor other evidence attributes ownership or control of the first-hop wallet to Pacific Meridian. No other material deficiency is intended.


Granite Coast Bank is filing this SAR on customer Alder Peak Equipment LLC and its majority owner, Samuel Brooks, age 51, of Spokane, Washington, regarding suspected movement of possible fraud proceeds through business checking account 58392017 and related cryptocurrency activity.

Alder Peak Equipment LLC opened business checking account 58392017 on September 8, 2024. At onboarding, Brooks described Alder Peak as a regional distributor of construction, forestry, and agricultural equipment parts. Brooks stated that the company purchased replacement components from domestic and overseas suppliers and sold primarily to contractors, equipment-repair shops, and agricultural businesses in Washington, Idaho, Oregon, and Montana.

Washington business records identified Alder Peak as an active limited liability company formed in 2019. Brooks was identified as a 70 percent owner and managing member. The remaining 30 percent was held by Rebecca Owens, age 47, of Coeur d’Alene, Idaho. Both individuals were identified and verified during account opening.

Alder Peak maintained a commercial warehouse and office in Spokane. The company provided business registration documents, tax records, supplier agreements, and commercial lease documentation during onboarding. Brooks estimated annual revenue of approximately $3.2 million and expected monthly account activity between $200,000 and $350,000.

From September 2024 through March 2026, account activity was generally consistent with the stated business profile. Alder Peak received ACH credits, checks, and domestic wires from recurring commercial customers and made payments to equipment manufacturers, freight companies, parts suppliers, payroll providers, tax authorities, utilities, insurance companies, and other business counterparties.

Typical monthly incoming activity ranged from approximately $190,000 to $330,000. Historical international wires were primarily sent to suppliers in Germany, Canada, Japan, and South Korea. Prior international payments generally ranged from $15,000 to $65,000 and were supported by recurring supplier relationships.

The bank identified no significant prior cryptocurrency-related activity in the account.

Beginning April 7, 2026, Granite Coast observed a material change in Alder Peak’s transaction activity.

Between April 7 and August 21, 2026, Alder Peak received 18 incoming domestic wires totaling $1,324,100 from 12 businesses that had not previously transacted with the customer.

