The sending businesses were located in nine states. Granite Coast identified no common ownership between Alder Peak and the originating companies through available customer information and public-record research.

Several senders operated in industries that did not appear directly related to Alder Peak’s historical construction and agricultural equipment business, including dental equipment, medical supply, office technology, and commercial interiors.

Within one to four business days of receiving 15 of the 18 incoming wires, Alder Peak sent funds to newly observed domestic and international counterparties.

Between April 8 and August 23, 2026, Alder Peak initiated 12 outgoing wires totaling $876,400.

The outgoing wires were:

April 8: $61,000 to Pacific Meridian Trading Ltd. in Hong Kong.
